---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import IndiaRegimeCalculator from '../../../../components/IndiaRegimeCalculator';
import { indiaRegimeRates as rates, estimateIndiaSalaryRegimes } from '../../../../calc/in/regimes';
import '../../../../styles/india-regime.css';
const money = (value: number) => new Intl.NumberFormat('en-IN', { style: 'currency', currency: 'INR', maximumFractionDigits: 0 }).format(value);
const schedules = [rates.old, rates.new];
const illustration = estimateIndiaSalaryRegimes({ annualSalary: 1500000, oldRegimeDeductions: 150000 });
const sources = [{ title: rates.source_title, url: rates.source_url }, { title: 'Finance Act 2026 — old-regime schedule and cess', url: rates.old.source_url }, { title: 'Income Tax Department — new Act scope and tax-year terminology', url: rates.year_source_url }];
---
<Base title="India Old vs New Regime Tax Calculator 2026–27 — Beta | CalcsDesk" description="Compare modeled old and new regime tax for a limited resident-under-60 salary case in Tax Year 2026–27. See deductions, rebate, marginal relief, cess and sources." breadcrumb="Income tax regime comparison" ancestors={[{ label: 'India', href: '/in/' }]} developmentMessage="India salary comparison beta · Enacted-source check; human review pending" application={{ name: 'India Salary Regime Comparison — Tax Year 2026–27', description: 'Limited annual ordinary-salary comparison for resident individuals under 60, with old-regime eligible deductions supplied by the user.' }}>
  <header class="india-intro"><p class="eyebrow">India / Ordinary salary / Tax Year 2026–27</p><h1>Old or new regime.<br /> <span class="accent">Compare the working.</span></h1><p class="lead">Compare modeled annual tax under both regimes for a resident individual under 60 with ordinary, fully taxable salary up to ₹50 lakh. Enter the same salary for both and the additional old-regime deductions you have separately confirmed are eligible.</p><p class="india-verification"><strong>Beta · Human review pending.</strong> Enacted-primary-source check: <time datetime={rates.verified_on}>{rates.verified_on}</time>. Tax Year {rates.tax_year}: {rates.effective_from} to {rates.effective_to}. <a href="#india-sources">View rates, source scope and review status ↓</a></p></header>
  <IndiaRegimeCalculator client:load />
  <noscript><section class="india-section"><h2>JavaScript is needed to change the comparison.</h2><p>The supported case, rate tables, method and source notes remain readable below.</p></section></noscript>
  <section class="india-section" aria-labelledby="india-scope-title"><p class="eyebrow">Check the supported case</p><h2 id="india-scope-title">Salary only. Confirm eligibility separately.</h2><ul><li>Resident individual under 60, with ordinary fully taxable salary as the only income. The tool does not determine residence, age-based eligibility or whether you can choose a regime.</li><li>Enter salary before the modeled standard deduction, not cost to company. Exempt salary components, HRA/LTA exemptions, taxable benefits and salary restructuring are outside this beta.</li><li>Additional old-regime deductions are a user-supplied, already-eligible aggregate. The tool does not validate individual deduction categories, conditions, documents or limits.</li><li>The new-regime calculation includes its standard deduction only. Employer pension contributions and other available adjustments are outside this version.</li><li>No capital gains, special-rate income, agricultural income, business/professional income, foreign income, loss adjustments or other income is modeled.</li><li>Salary is limited to ₹50 lakh. Surcharge, higher-income cases, non-residents, senior-citizen schedules, interest, penalties and tax already paid or withheld are outside the result.</li></ul><p>The comparison identifies a lower modeled amount for these assumptions. It is not a personal regime recommendation, a return-preparation service, a withholding figure or a refund estimate.</p></section>
  <section class="india-section" aria-labelledby="india-method-title"><p class="eyebrow">Follow each step</p><h2 id="india-method-title">Deductions, slabs, rebate, then cess.</h2><p>The old regime subtracts a standard deduction of up to {money(rates.old.standard_deduction)} and the eligible additional deductions you enter. The new regime subtracts a standard deduction of up to {money(rates.new.standard_deduction)}. Neither standard deduction exceeds the salary.</p><p>After statutory taxable-income rounding, each regime applies its own slab rates. In the supported resident case, the old-regime rebate is up to {money(rates.old.rebate_max)} at taxable income up to {money(rates.old.rebate_threshold)}. The new-regime rebate is up to {money(rates.new.rebate_max)} at taxable income up to {money(rates.new.rebate_threshold)}.</p><p>Above the new-regime rebate threshold, the supported marginal-relief calculation reduces pre-cess tax where applicable so that it does not exceed income above that threshold. The model does not apply corresponding old-regime rebate marginal relief. {rates.cess.rate_bps / 100}% Health and Education Cess follows rebate and relief. Total income and final tax are rounded to the nearest ₹{rates.rounding.multiple}, ignoring paise first, with a last rupee digit of five rounding up.</p><p>The source framework is the Income-tax Act, 2025 as amended by Finance Act, 2026. This page uses “Tax Year 2026–27” for income from 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027. AY 2026–27 filing guidance describes the previous income year and is not used as the primary basis for this model.</p></section>
  <section class="india-section" aria-labelledby="india-example-title"><p class="eyebrow">CalcsDesk arithmetic illustration</p><h2 id="india-example-title">₹15 lakh salary, ₹1.5 lakh eligible additional old-regime deductions.</h2><p>For these illustrative inputs, the modeled rounded old-regime annual tax is {money(illustration.old.totalTax)} and new-regime annual tax is {money(illustration.new.totalTax)}, including cess. The entered additional deductions are assumed eligible; this example does not establish their availability.</p><p>This is our illustration generated by the model, not an official government worked example. Current-tax-year full official worked-example checks and human review remain pending.</p></section>
  <section id="india-sources" class="india-section" aria-labelledby="india-rates-title"><p class="eyebrow">Look behind the comparison</p><h2 id="india-rates-title">Tax Year {rates.tax_year} rates and sources.</h2><p>Effective {rates.effective_from} to {rates.effective_to}. {rates.verified_by}. Source-check record: {rates.verified_on}. Rate-table bounds are annual taxable income after deductions and statutory rounding.</p>{schedules.map(schedule => <div><h3>{schedule.label}</h3><div class="india-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${schedule.label} annual taxable-income slab rates`}><table><caption>{schedule.label} · annual taxable income</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Above</th><th scope="col">Up to</th><th scope="col">Rate on this slab</th></tr></thead><tbody>{schedule.brackets.map((band, index) => <tr><td>{money(index === 0 ? 0 : schedule.brackets[index - 1].up_to!)}</td><td>{band.up_to === null ? 'No upper slab bound' : money(band.up_to)}</td><td>{band.rate_bps / 100}%</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>Source: <a href={schedule.source_url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{schedule.source_title} ↗<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>. Checked {schedule.verified_on}; {schedule.verified_by}.</p></div>)}<ul>{sources.map(source => <li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.title} ↗<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>)}</ul><p>{rates.worked_example_status}</p><p>A source check is distinct from human or professional review. This searchable beta retains its incomplete review gates; search eligibility is not verification.</p></section>
  <section class="india-section" aria-labelledby="india-faq-title"><h2 id="india-faq-title">Before using the comparison.</h2><details><summary>Does lower modeled tax mean I should choose that regime?</summary><p>No. It only compares the two results for the supported salary case and your entered deduction aggregate. Eligibility, exemptions, other income, available deductions and filing choices require separate consideration.</p></details><details><summary>Does this check whether my deductions are allowed?</summary><p>No. You must establish the additional old-regime deduction amount independently, including relevant category limits and conditions. The tool only limits that aggregate to salary remaining after its standard deduction.</p></details><details><summary>Why can salary above ₹12 lakh still have no modeled new-regime tax?</summary><p>The rebate threshold applies to rounded taxable income, after the supported standard deduction, rather than salary before that deduction. The result shows the taxable amount, rebate and any applicable marginal relief separately.</p></details><details><summary>Are my salary inputs submitted or saved?</summary><p>The calculation runs in your browser. This tool has no salary submission endpoint, automatic storage or share-link feature. Refreshing restores the initial illustrative inputs.</p></details></section>
  <nav class="india-related" aria-label="Related pages"><a href="/in/">India tools ↗</a><a href="/methodology/">How we test ↗</a><a href="/team/">Review status ↗</a></nav>
</Base>
